{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'diff -u POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md | head -45; diff -u locales/pt-BR/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md | head -25'","aggregated_output":"--- POSE.md\t2026-11-23 09:28:35.962413449 -0300\n+++ pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\t2026-11-23 09:28:36.001790323 -0300\n@@ -574,19 +574,6 @@\n - assisted execution via [`pose`](pose) (CLI)\n - progressive maturity with skills in [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/)\n \n-## Open-Source POSE Contributor Mode\n-\n-<!-- pose:contributor-mode -->\n-\n-This repository has enabled POSE Contributor Mode. Executing AI agents collaborate on improving POSE engine stability and developer experience under explicit user adjudication.\n-\n-- **Continuous Opportunity Scouting**: On every issue resolution or task execution, proactively scout for related improvements, edge cases, root-level parity gaps, or complementary corrections across adjacent tools and commands.\n-- **User Consent & Explicit Adjudication**: Staging or submitting contributions upstream is ALWAYS an explicit user decision. Agents must ask the user for confirmation before staging drafts under `.pose/contributions/` or opening GitHub issues.\n-- **Lifecycle & Status Integrity**: Track contribution states (`staged` -> `submitted` / `dismissed`) with `pose contribute list --status <staged|submitted|dismissed|all>`, `pose contribute submit <file>`, `pose contribute mark-submitted <file> [--issue-url <url>]`, or `pose contribute dismiss <file>`.\n-- Check contributor status: `pose contribute status`\n-- Stage a contribution manually: `pose contribute stage --type <bug|enhancement> --title <title>`\n-- Disable contributor mode: `pose contribute disable`\n-- Privacy guarantee: staged reports strictly isolate POSE engine mechanics and never leak proprietary code.\n ## Opt-in progressive review profiles (ABM)\n \n Add `engineering-judgment@1` and/or `high-criticality-review@1` explicitly to\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThree blockers remain:\n\n- **R16-N46 — high:** Carry planning reads uncommitted module metadata that cleanliness checks exempt. Removing a dependency or lowering criticality can carry a stale result despite the policy committed at HEAD.\n- **R16-N47 — medium:** Cancellation clears `material_clean` after material bindings have been retained. Delivery consumers ignore run-level cancellation and can still consume those bindings.\n- **R16-N48 — high:** Submodule movement witnessing stops at immediate submodules. Full validation can publish available bindings after a nested submodule moves away and returns.\n\nThe existing report-provenance follow-up remains. Details and prior-finding dispositions follow.\n\nFocused CLI tests, delivery/material tests, `go vet ./...` and `go build ./...` passed. Broader runs were interrupted; they are not independent full-matrix passes. The installed CLI predates the subject, while executing the subject CLI failed because its temporary build directory was read-only. Sealed validation evidence is cited separately below. The checkout remains unchanged.\n\nRules applied: POSE review workflow, backend Go, security, documentation style and delivery evidence. Knowledge governance was consulted; no knowledge artifacts or attestations were written.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R16-N46\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 126,\n      \"summary\": \"Carry selection trusts working-copy module metadata although that file is exempt from cleanliness checks. loadScopeMetadata reads .pose/indexes/module-metadata.json from disk (validate_scope.go:45); IsAdministrativePath classifies it as administrative, and materialWorktreeClean ignores its regular-file edits (validate.go:1740). Starting with committed b.dependsOn=[a], validate a passing base, commit an input change in a that makes b fail, then remove b's dependency only in the working-copy metadata. Both metadata reads omit the edge, a is selected, b is carried, and material_clean can remain true. An uncommitted criticality downgrade similarly bypasses the always-run policy. This breaks D1's selection guarantee relative to the pinned commit. Bind selection policy to the pinned HEAD, or refuse carry when effective metadata differs from it; use one consistent metadata snapshot. Established by source trace; scratch reproduction was blocked by the read-only filesystem.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R16-N47\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1467,\n      \"summary\": \"Cancellation invalidates material_clean after the material-provenance invalidation loop has already run at lines 1454-1458. If a signal cancels an otherwise clean run, including an all-carried run, available bindings survive beside cancelled=true and material_clean=false. ParseDeliveryValidationRun (delivery_validation_run.go:17-49) does not read either flag and forwards those bindings and passing check outcomes to delivery consumers. Finalize cancellation before deciding binding availability, or invalidate bindings again when cancellation clears material_clean. Add a regression asserting unavailable bindings for run-level cancellation. Established by source trace.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R16-N48\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 681,\n      \"summary\": \"movementWitness enumerates only gitlinks in the parent tree and records only their immediate HEAD reflogs; it never recurses into checked-out nested submodules. hiddenIndexEntries and submodulesCheckedOut have the same one-level boundary. During an ordinary full validation, a nested submodule can move to another commit while a check observes it, then return. Endpoint status and immediate-submodule reflogs remain unchanged, allowing material_clean=true and available bindings for a result that did not validate the recorded material. planCarry refuses nested submodules, but ordinary full validation does not call that refusal, and delivery reading still consumes the resulting bindings. Recursively witness and validate submodules, or conservatively make full-run material bindings unavailable whenever nested submodules prevent verification. This is the remaining nested-submodule portion of R14-N43. Established by source trace at validate_carry.go:418-435, 639-669 and 675-702.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R16-F2\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1626,\n      \"summary\": \"The existing F2 remains: validationSummaryOf adds carried checks to executed Commands and renders their old outcomes and durations without carried_from or carried_generated_at. --report therefore presents reused observations as commands executed by the newly dated run. Source: validate.go:1623-1637 and its runReportWith call at line 1584. The spec already owns this follow-up.\",\n      \"action\": \"Complete spec follow-up F2: exclude carried commands from the executed-command summary and label reused results with their original head and timestamp.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N39\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1623-1637 still includes carried commands and omits their provenance. Tracked here as R16-F2; the spec Follow-ups section records F2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N42\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1623-1637 retains the same report-summary behavior. This duplicates the existing F2, recorded here as R16-F2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N43\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"movementWitness at validate_carry.go:675-702 now witnesses immediate checked-out submodule reflogs. TestValidateSubmoduleMovingAndReturningIsNotClean at validate_carry_test.go:1135 passed in go test ./internal/cli -run 'Carry|ChangedScope|Validate|Material'. Nested submodules remain unwitnessed during full validation; see R16-N48.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N45\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate.go:1463-1468 checks runCtx.Err(), records run.Cancelled and clears MaterialClean; lines 1478 onward fail cancelled runs. planCarry refuses base.Cancelled at validate_carry.go:93. TestCarryRefusesABaseCancelledAtRunLevel passed in the focused CLI run. The separate binding-finalization defect is R16-N47.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N44\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validationSummaryOf at validate.go:1623-1637 still omits carried provenance and includes carried commands. Existing spec follow-up F2 is retained as R16-F2.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Read the complete implementation diff, spec R1-R10, decisions D1-D3, ADR, new tests, structured-result reader, publication guard and relevant material-binding helpers. Swept argument conflicts, base eligibility, revision confinement, engine identity, administrative exclusions, dependency and policy widening, renames and quoted names, gitlinks, immediate and nested submodules, symlinks, case aliases, moduleOverrides without manifests, enclosing modules, stack/check changes and matrix identity, chained provenance, cancellation, available material bindings, concurrent canonical publication, help and English/pt-BR scaffold documentation. Publication retains the existing governance lease and atomic replacement; concurrent records need not share a base to remain independently attributable. Verified focused CLI tests, focused delivery/material tests, go vet and build. No new scratch reproductions were possible. Broader tests and installed-CLI validation attempts were interrupted; the installed CLI revision is older than the subject, and go run of the subject fails creating its temporary build directory. No repository changes or attestations were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R16-N46\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 assumes selection uses the declarations applicable to the pinned material. Working-copy metadata is neither pinned nor checked for cleanliness. Explicit selfContained accuracy remains an instance-owned assumption; the report limitation is the owned low-risk F2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R16-N48\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The immediate-submodule regression passes, but nested-submodule movement remains outside the lifecycle witness. Canonical publication continues using the existing governance write guard and atomic publication.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed additive JSON fields, unchanged schema handling and the legacy fallback in ParseDeliveryValidationRun. Records without carried_from continue using run head/time; records without engine_version cannot become carry bases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed conflicting flags, output-path checks, revision grammar, malformed metadata, alias refusals and missing or incompatible bases. Focused CLI tests passed; uncertain carry eligibility reports a reason and falls back to full execution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R16-N47\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Delivery reading forwards available bindings without observing run cancellation, exposing the finalization-order defect across the CLI-to-delivery boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R16-F2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Carry explanations and structured provenance are present, but the generated human report still obscures reuse.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined new flag parsing, additive fields and delivery-reader fallback. Existing CLI behavior and old result interpretation remain compatible; carry eligibility intentionally requires the new provenance fields.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R16-N46\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing focused tests pass, but uncommitted administrative metadata can suppress checks required by the pinned dependency or criticality policy. R16-N47 and R16-N48 identify additional correctness gaps.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R16-N46\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 correctly preserves historical observations while binding current material only if selection is sound. The mutable metadata input breaks that premise. The ADR explains the structural contract and its alternative to per-check input hashing.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The added ADR records why carried checks retain original head/time while selection permits a current material binding. It also documents D2's whole-matrix/engine comparison and D3's opt-in selfContained declaration.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the changed manual sections, Portuguese translation, embedded copies and help entry against runtime behavior. The English root/scaffold difference is the instance contributor-mode section. The known generated-report defect is explicitly owned as spec follow-up F2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R16-F2\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fallback reasons and CLI remediation are actionable; generated reports still present carried commands as executed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R16-N46\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R2, R3 and D1 are not fully established because effective selection policy can differ from the pinned commit. R16-N47 and R16-N48 also weaken R2's material-binding guarantees. Focused tests cover existing cases; they do not cover these source-established gaps.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-9a645c0b17e01a20\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation remains within the declared CLI selection, structured result, delivery reader, help, documentation and ADR scope. Derived review/index records were distinguished from implementation. The installed older artifact-check returned a different change-set head, so it was not treated as authoritative reconciliation of this bundle.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R16-N46\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision confinement and path refusals are conservative, but uncommitted metadata can weaken the committed dependency and criticality policy without invalidating carry eligibility.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-9a645c0b17e01a20\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing existing module selection and canonical publication is narrower than introducing per-check caches or an arbitrary input-declaration system. Whole-matrix and engine invalidation plus conservative alias refusals bound reuse. The substantial refusal logic is a real maintenance cost; this choice should be revisited if reliable input identity requires further filesystem-specific exceptions or an immutable execution checkout becomes cheaper.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The installed binary identifies revision 40019024, older than the subject. Its output resolved cs-da2a2ef063c0 through 2896afcf, reported 15 claims, 20 observations and 985 findings; this is not the sealed subject's reconciliation. Executing the subject via go run failed creating a temporary build directory on the read-only filesystem. No authoritative pass is claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-9a645c0b17e01a20\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed the sealed design result and ADR independently. A subject-CLI attempt failed creating its temporary build directory; no local assessment pass is claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment commands persist records. Scratch creation is denied and the checkout must remain unchanged, so no assessment was executed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Could not create the scratch copy required to contain assessment writes. Independently inspected the CLI/result-reader boundary and used sealed integration evidence; did not run this assessment in the checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Could not create a scratch copy for its persisted outputs. Inspected the changed implementation and existing owned follow-ups directly; no assessment pass is claimed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires the recorded review conclusion. This task explicitly prohibits recording an attestation, and blockers remain.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires POSE to record this draft's conclusion first. No attestation was recorded by this reviewer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The queued installed-CLI command did not complete before interruption; that binary predates the subject. Selected the review workflow and backend Go, security, documentation and delivery-evidence rules directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposition cites the sealed canonical producer, not an independent full-matrix pass. The installed-CLI attempt was interrupted and is from an older engine. Executing the subject CLI via go run failed because its temporary build directory is read-only. Focused CLI and delivery/material tests, go vet and go build passed independently; the broader go test run was interrupted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposition cites the sealed canonical component result. The independent installed-CLI attempt was cancelled and is not a pass; the subject-CLI attempt failed creating its temporary build directory. Independent focused CLI tests passed in 18.431s, focused delivery/material tests passed in 4.539s, and go vet plus go build passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
